# Always commit and push after each change

When a meaningful change set is finished (feature, fix, UI, deploy sync, rules, etc.):

1. **Commit** all related files for that change (do not leave finished work uncommitted).
2. **Push** to the tracked remote branch immediately after a successful commit (`git push` / `git push -u origin HEAD` if needed).
3. Follow the repo’s existing Git Safety Protocol (no force push to main/master, no config changes, no skipping hooks, HEREDOC commit messages).
4. Do this even when the user did not separately ask to commit/push — this standing preference overrides the default “only commit when asked” behavior for this project.

Whitespace-only or accidental touch with no real change does not need a commit.
